cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VideoGenDoctor in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "VideoGenDoctor: Structured Diagnosis, Evidence Localization, and Repair for Controllable Video Generation"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/tanbo1217/videogendoctor"
abstract: >
  VideoGenDoctor is a closed-loop failure diagnosis and repair system for
  controllable video generation. It replaces scalar quality scores with
  structured diagnosis records — each carrying a taxonomy code, temporal
  evidence span, affected target, confidence, representative keyframes, and
  a compiled repair action. The pipeline combines lightweight feature-based
  screening, optional structured VLM verification, and a template-driven
  patch compiler.
